  "definition_audit": "First thirteen actual path literals identical97; R and positive-part rate literal; U_y=V+norm(x-y)^2/(2 eta)+norm(p)^2/2; real-time clamp identical94. A=Gamma(T), Iplus integrates rate(gamma), Iminus integrates rate(R gamma) along the same path, not reversed time. Exact simplex m retained unused; no normalization hypothesis.",
  "core_delta": "Both actual whole-path rate integrabilities, U_y(A)-U_y(z)=Iplus-Iminus, and exp(-U_y(z))*exp(-Iplus)=exp(-U_y(A))*exp(-Iminus) for every finite prescribed tuple and nonnegative horizon.",
  "consumer": "Weighted prescribed-sector Theta balance requires this finite Gibbs/survival identity together with separate reverse-arc and event-rate product correspondence, actual94 density and97 volume substitution; Gibbs probability averaging follows later.",
  "truth_boundary": "No equality of reversed right-continuous jump values, no reversed-event density balance, weighted Theta preservation, stationary averaging/invariance, Markovness, hypocoercivity, errors, expected cost, main result or composition.",
